BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artist-in-Residence Lecture | Alex Krueger @ CMoG
DTSTART:20260903T220000Z
DTEND:20260903T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260904T133027Z
UID:cc37c7312b072051e76fdc462931d49b30f4c932@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Glass
DESCRIPTION:Artist-in-Residence Lecture | Alex Krueger\nSeptember 3\, 2026
  6:00 pm–7:00 pm EDT\nStudio Theater\nJoin us in The Studio Theater for 
 Alex Krueger's Artist-in-Residence lecture where he will describe his work
  and residency project. Krueger is a Brooklyn-based glass artist whose pra
 ctice explores glass as a fractured language\, merging hot-sculpted parts
 \, blow molds\, and faux mosaic techniques to create layered\, improvisati
 onal forms.\nKrueger will use his residency to continue his exploration on
  how new technologies—facial recognition\, autonomous vehicles\, and our
  closely held personal devices— embed systems of surveillance within the
 ir function that influence our behavior. Using The Studio’s array of gla
 ssmaking equipment\, facilities\, and its community of talented glass work
 ers\, he will further develop the scale and ambition of his practice.\nRes
 ervations for this event are not required. This lecture is free and open t
 o the public.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/e
 vent/78439054/20260903180000
GEO:42.1498;77.0542
LOCATION:Corning Museum of Glass\, One Museum Way\, Corning\, NY\, 14830
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78439054/20260903180000
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artist-in-Residence Lecture | Jinya Zhao @ CMoG
DTSTART:20260903T220000Z
DTEND:20260903T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260904T133027Z
UID:e6d9c6efec302f8ead0b135d0c75fe43cf4baefc@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Glass
DESCRIPTION:Artist-in-Residence Lecture | Jinya Zhao\nSeptember 3\, 2026 6
 :00 pm–7:00 pm EDT\nStudio Theater\nJoin us in The Studio Theater for Ji
 nya Zhao's Artist-in-Residence lecture. Zhao is currently a PhD candidate 
 at the Royal College of Art in London\, pursuing doctoral research that in
 troduces the concept of "synaesthetic touch\," proposing that blown glass 
 can bridge visual\, tactile\, and spatial sensory experiences to deepen au
 dience engagement. Her research also examines "layerspace"—the interplay
  between depth\, structure\, and spatial narratives—and "site\," conside
 ring how environmental and cultural contexts influence the reception of gl
 ass works.\nHer residency at The Studio provides Zhao with the opportunity
  to create a new body of blown glass work expanding on these concepts.\nRe
 servations for this event are not required. This lecture is free and open 
 to the public.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/
 event/78439053/20260903180000
GEO:42.1498;77.0542
LOCATION:Corning Museum of Glass\, One Museum Way\, Corning\, NY\, 14830
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78439053/20260903180000
END:VEVENT
